# P25 (docs/RISK.md V267-V271): a GenericIon beam in the B1 sweep's shape - C12 at 1 GeV per
# nucleon, 50,000 events, QBBC as it ships on the Geant4 side (ref/B1build's exampleB1, or
# ref\b1ion\run.bat for the same dose with ionElastic counted).
#
# THE PORT CANNOT FIRE IT, and refuses it by name: `G4RunManager::CheckSpecies` stops a
# GenericIon primary because this port's gun has no `/gun/ion Z A` and its seeding kernel
# (`seed_track_slot`, called from src/host/transport_run_impl.cuh) writes `ion_za = 0` for every
# primary - so the nuclide has nowhere to come from. P25 may not edit the host engine; the C12 row
# is Geant4's alone until a package gives the gun a nuclide.
/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/gun/particle ion
/gun/ion 6 12
/gun/energy 12000 MeV
/run/printProgress 5000
/run/beamOn 50000
